Aim - Information Gathering using Google Search Techniques of Google Search Engine

Theory - Google Dorking is the use of advanced Google search operators to find specific information from publicly indexed web pages.
         It helps in passive information gathering because it does not directly interact with the target system.

Google Search Operators:

1. site:
— Restricts search results to a specific website or domain.
Example - site:wikipedia.org artificial intelligence
           — Searches for artificial intelligence only on Wikipedia.
          site:.gov.in cybersecurity
           — Searches for cybersecurity on Indian government websites.

2. filetype:
— Restricts the result to a specific file format.
Example - site:nasa.gov filetype:pdf climate
           — Finds PDF documents related to climate on NASA's website.
          filetype:xls "annual report"
           — Searches for Excel spreadsheet files containing the phrase "annual report".

3. intitle:
— Searches for a word or exact phrase within the webpage title.
Example - intitle:"index of" "parent directory"
           — Searches for pages that contain "index of" in the title and "parent directory" in the page content.
          intitle:"cyber security"
           — Finds pages containing the phrase "cyber security" in the title.

4. allintitle:
— Searches for pages whose titles contain all the specified words.
Example - allintitle: annual report 2025
           — Finds pages whose titles contain "annual", "report", and "2025".

5. inurl:
— Searches for a word or phrase within the webpage URL.
Example - inurl:admin site:*.in
           — Finds websites whose URL contains the word "admin".
          inurl:login site:.edu
           — Finds educational websites whose URL contains the word "login".

6. allinurl:
— Searches for URLs containing all the specified words.
Example - allinurl: contact whatsapp
           — Searches for URLs containing both "contact" and "whatsapp".

7. intext:
— Searches for a specific word or phrase within the body text of webpages/documents.
Example - intext:"cyber security" "budget"
           — Finds documents containing the words "cyber security" and "budget".
          intext:"cyber security"
           — Finds webpages containing the phrase "cyber security".

8. allintext:
— Searches for webpages containing all the specified words in their body text.
Example - allintext: annual report 2025
           — Finds pages whose body text contains "annual", "report", and "2025".

9. - (Minus Operator)
— Excludes a specified word from the search results.
Example - python -snake
           — Searches for Python while excluding results related to snakes.

10. related:
— Finds websites related or similar to a specified website.
Example - related:wikipedia.org, related:github.com
           — Finds websites related or similar to the specified website.
